{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj55h37QzVS5Sz94Rpx3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient, immense, and utterly plain.*\n\n*No handle. No keyhole. No hinges visible.*\n\n*You said \"key.\"*\n\n*The wood grain shifts. Letters bleed through the surface like old ink rising through water:*\n\n---\n\n**Which door did you name?**\n\n*I am every door and no door. I am the concept of threshold itself — the membrane between where you are and where you mean to be.*\n\n*You brought a key, but you haven't told me which lock I wear.*\n\n*Name me, and I will become.*\n\n---\n\n*The grain settles. The door waits. It is patient in the way only something made of dead wood and living possibility can be patient.*\n\n*Behind it, you hear everything. Or nothing. It's hard to tell the difference through a door that doesn't know what it is yet.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":197,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}